  "components": [
    {
      "id": "warning-shader",
      "explanation": "The hand-written canvas_item shader that turns a spike trap red, and the trap whose state drives it. One Sprite2D, one material, one line inside fragment(). The state machine owns warn_amount and the shader only reads it.",
      "beat_ids": [
        "B02",
        "B03"
      ],
      "files": [
        "shaders/trap_warning.gdshader",
        "features/traps/spike_trap.gd",
        "features/traps/spike_trap.tscn"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "material-driver",
      "explanation": "Agent-written presentation. Duplicates the ShaderMaterial per trap instance so three traps do not share one warn_amount, asks the shader at startup whether the uniform it is about to write exists, and copies state into that uniform once a frame after the state machine has run.",
      "beat_ids": [
        "B04",
        "B05"
      ],
      "files": [
        "features/traps/trap_warning_driver.gd",
        "tests/test_trap_shader_driver.gd"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "hint-experiment",
      "explanation": "One unshaded spatial shader with two samplers bound to the same three-pixel file, differing only by source_color, and a bool that picks which reaches ALBEDO. The scene fixes the pipeline the measurement depends on: Linear tonemap at exposure 1.0, no light, every post effect off.",
      "beat_ids": [
        "B06",
        "B07",
        "B10",
        "B11"
      ],
      "files": [
        "shaders/hint_bands.gdshader",
        "scenes/hint_experiment.tscn",
        "assets/materials/hint_with_source_color.tres",
        "assets/materials/hint_without_source_color.tres",
        "assets/textures/hint_bands.png",
        "assets/textures/hint_bands.png.import",
        "tools/write_textures.gd",
        "tools/capture_hint.gd"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "textured-surface",
      "explanation": "The hand-written spatial shader, its colour and data samplers and four grouped parameters, with two materials that differ in three values. One slime takes its material from the importer so a reimport keeps it; the other overrides at the node, so the pair is identical geometry under identical light.",
      "beat_ids": [
        "B08",
        "B09"
      ],
      "files": [
        "shaders/dungeon_surface.gdshader",
        "assets/materials/stone_dry.tres",
        "assets/materials/stone_flooded.tres",
        "assets/textures/stone_albedo.png",
        "assets/textures/stone_albedo.png.import",
        "assets/textures/wetness_mask.png",
        "assets/textures/wetness_mask.png.import",
        "scenes/asset_showcase.tscn",
        "assets/models/slime.glb",
        "assets/models/slime.glb.import",
        "tools/capture_materials.gd",
        "tests/test_materials.gd"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "the-room",
      "explanation": "What the shader is attached to and what drives it in play: the three-trap room, the player who can only walk and jump, the code-drawn sprites the pixel predictions were written against, and the project settings that fix the renderer and resolution.",
      "beat_ids": [
        "B03",
        "B05"
      ],
      "files": [
        "game/main.tscn",
        "game/main.gd",
        "features/player/player.gd",
        "features/player/player.tscn",
        "assets/sprites/spike_trap.png",
        "assets/sprites/spike_trap.png.import",
        "assets/sprites/spike_trap_fired.png",
        "assets/sprites/spike_trap_fired.png.import",
        "assets/sprites/player.png",
        "assets/sprites/player.png.import",
        "assets/sprites/floor_tile.png",
        "assets/sprites/floor_tile.png.import",
        "project.godot",
        "tools/capture_rig.gd"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "evidence-harness",
      "explanation": "What the claims rest on. The state suite at three pinned frame rates, the input-map check, Assignment 3's geometry check carried across, and the capture driver that records the warning as real motion and asserts its own outcome before a frame counts as evidence.",
      "beat_ids": [
        "B03",
        "B05",
        "B12"
      ],
      "files": [
        "tests/test_trap_warning.gd",
        "tests/test_input_map.gd",
        "tests/check_assets_3d.gd",
        "tests/capture_shader.gd"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "generated-reference",
      "explanation": "Godot's own output, produced by converting a StandardMaterial3D with albedo, normal-map and roughness textures enabled. Nothing loads it. It is in the project to be read: its line 7 marks the albedo sampler as colour and its line 19 leaves the normal map as data, which is the distinction the hand-written shader makes on its own lines 3 and 4.",
      "beat_ids": [
        "B10"
      ],
      "files": [
        "shaders/standard_generated.gdshader"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "excerpts": [
    {
      "beat_id": "B02",
      "path": "shaders/trap_warning.gdshader",
      "start_line": 1,
      "end_line": 7,
      "text": "shader_type canvas_item;\nuniform float warn_amount : hint_range(0.0, 1.0) = 0.0;\nuniform vec3 warn_color: source_color = vec3(0.839216, 0.235294, 0.184314);\n\nvoid fragment(){\nCOLOR.rgb = mix(COLOR.rgb, warn_color, warn_amount);\n}"
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B04",
      "path": "features/traps/trap_warning_driver.gd",
      "start_line": 62,
      "end_line": 76,
      "text": "\t# R6. duplicate() is shallow, which is what is wanted: the Shader itself\n\t# stays shared (it is read-only program text) while the parameter block\n\t# becomes this trap's own.\n\tmaterial = shared.duplicate() as ShaderMaterial\n\t_sprite.material = material\n\n\tuniform_declared = _declares(material.shader, UNIFORM_WARN)\n\tif not uniform_declared:\n\t\tpush_error(\"Shader does not declare a uniform named '%s'; every write from this driver would be discarded in silence.\" % UNIFORM_WARN)\n\n\nfunc _process(_delta: float) -> void:\n\tif material == null:\n\t\treturn\n\tmaterial.set_shader_parameter(UNIFORM_WARN, _trap.warn_amount)"
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B06",
      "path": "shaders/hint_bands.gdshader",
      "start_line": 1,
      "end_line": 7,
      "text": "shader_type spatial;\nrender_mode unshaded;\n\nuniform sampler2D bands_srgb : source_color, filter_nearest;\nuniform sampler2D bands_data : filter_nearest;\n\nuniform bool use_source_color = true;"
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B08",
      "path": "shaders/dungeon_surface.gdshader",
      "start_line": 15,
      "end_line": 27,
      "text": "void fragment() {\n\t// 遮罩：0 表示干燥，1 表示完全湿润。\n\tfloat w = texture(wetness_mask, UV).r;\n\n\t// 石头本色乘上颜色调整。\n\tvec3 base = texture(stone_albedo, UV).rgb * tint;\n\n\t// 越湿越暗。\n\tALBEDO = base * (1.0 - w * water_darkening);\n\n\t// 根据湿度，在干燥和湿润粗糙度之间插值。\n\tROUGHNESS = mix(roughness_dry, water_roughness, w);\n}"
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B10",
      "path": "shaders/hint_bands.gdshader",
      "start_line": 4,
      "end_line": 5,
      "text": "uniform sampler2D bands_srgb : source_color, filter_nearest;\nuniform sampler2D bands_data : filter_nearest;"
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B11A",
      "path": "shaders/standard_generated.gdshader",
      "start_line": 3,
      "end_line": 12,
      "text": "shader_type spatial;\nrender_mode blend_mix, depth_draw_opaque, cull_back, diffuse_burley, specular_schlick_ggx;\n\nuniform vec4 albedo : source_color;\nuniform sampler2D texture_albedo : source_color, filter_linear_mipmap, repeat_enable;\nuniform ivec2 albedo_texture_size;\nuniform float point_size : hint_range(0.1, 128.0, 0.1);\n\nuniform float roughness : hint_range(0.0, 1.0);\nuniform sampler2D texture_metallic : hint_default_white, filter_linear_mipmap, repeat_enable;"
    }
  ],
